post.description:
Expects a name (unique within the event) and optional description, e.g. "Under 20" or "21km".
Returns 201 with the category; 400 for validation errors; 401 if not logged in;
403 if not an Organiser or not the event's owner; 404 if the event does not exist; 409 if the name is taken.

put.description:
Expects a name and optional description.
Returns 200 with the updated category; 400 for validation errors; 401 if not logged in;
403 if not an Organiser or not the owner; 404 if not found; 409 if the name is taken within the event.

post.description:
Expects the id of one of the event's categories. Records the link between the participant, the event and
the category. Returns 201 with the enrolment; 400 for validation errors or a category from another event;
401 if not logged in; 403 if not a Participant; 404 if the event does not exist;
409 if already enrolled in this event.

put.description:
Expects the same fields as creating an event.
Returns 200 with the updated event; 400 for validation errors; 401 if not logged in;
403 if not an Organiser or not the event's owner; 404 if the event does not exist.

post.description:
Expects an enrolment id (which must belong to this event), a finish time (hh:mm:ss) and a finish position.
Returns 201 with the result; 400 for validation errors or an enrolment from another event;
401 if not logged in; 403 if not an Organiser or not the event's owner; 404 if the event does not exist;
409 if a result was already captured for that enrolment.

put.description:
Expects a finish time (hh:mm:ss) and a finish position.
Returns 200 with the updated result; 400 for validation errors; 401 if not logged in;
403 if not an Organiser or not the event's owner; 404 if the result does not exist.
